Created by Claude.ai from hippoplayerupdate.readme

==============================================================================
HIPPOPLAYER USER GUIDE - New Features (through v2.67)
==============================================================================

TABLE OF CONTENTS

  1.  Getting Started / Installation
  2.  List Modes
  3.  Favorites
  4.  File Browser
  5.  Search View (Internet Search & Shared Playlists)
  6.  Downloading Files
  7.  Streaming MP3 & Radio Stations
  8.  Window & Font Customization
  9.  Position Slider & Play Mode Button
  10. Scopes (Visualizers)
  11. SID / PSID Playback
  12. High-Quality XM Playback (xmaplay)
  13. MIDI Playback
  14. Console/Chiptune Music (vgm2wav, mdx2wav)
  15. MP3 via External Hardware (MHI)
  16. AmiGUS Hardware Mixing
  17. Trinity Accelerator Audio
  18. Metadata & Song Length Database
  19. New Supported Music Formats
  20. Keyboard Shortcuts Reference

==============================================================================
1. GETTING STARTED / INSTALLATION
==============================================================================

- Copy the HiP binary anywhere you like, and copy
  "HippoPlayer.group" to S: (or next to the HiP binary if you're on
  Kickstart 2.0+; the location can also be set in Prefs).
- You can copy these files over an existing installation.
- Requires "reqtools.library" to be installed.
- If you only need Protracker playback, the .group file isn't
  required.
- IMPORTANT: always update HippoPlayer.group alongside the binary --
  old group files are incompatible with new versions.

==============================================================================
2. LIST MODES
==============================================================================

Use the list mode toggle button (top of the file slider) or press
[SHIFT+M] to cycle between:

- Main list     - your working playlist
- Favorites     - modules you've favorited
- File browser  - browse your file system for modules
- Search view   - search internet sites and browse shared playlists

==============================================================================
3. FAVORITES
==============================================================================

- Right-click a module in the list to toggle its favorite status
  (favorited items show in bold).
- Shortcut: [CTRL+F].
- Enable this feature via Prefs > General > Favorites.
- Favorites are saved automatically to S:HippoFavorites.prg.
- The currently playing subsong is remembered per favorite, so it
  resumes on that subsong next time.
- A confirmation dialog protects you from accidentally
  clearing/editing the favorites list.

==============================================================================
4. FILE BROWSER
==============================================================================

- Switch to this mode to browse directories directly for modules.
- Enter/Return, the Play button, or double-click opens a directory.
- The top list entry represents "go to parent" -- or press
  [BACKSPACE].
- Files are filtered by Prefs > Loading > File Match Pattern.
- Enable Prefs > General > Keep list on exit to return to the same
  directory (and list position) next time you start Hippo.
- Drag-and-drop of folders onto the Hippo window is supported
  (recursively scanned).

==============================================================================
5. SEARCH VIEW (INTERNET SEARCH & SHARED PLAYLISTS)
==============================================================================

Requires UHCTools installed for internet connectivity.

- Switch to the Search view (list mode button, or [CTRL+S]).
- Pick a search source from the source button, type your query, and
  press Enter.
- Available sources include Modland, Aminet, Modules.pl, HVSC, AMP
  (Amiga Music Preservation), amigaremix.com, remix.kwed.org, radio
  stations, and Shared Playlists (community-curated lists, e.g.
  favorite/top lists).
- Your last-used search source is remembered in Prefs.

==============================================================================
6. DOWNLOADING FILES
==============================================================================

- From the File Browser or Search view, select an item and click Add
  (or press [A]) to copy it into your main playlist.
- To download a remote file to local disk, press [CTRL+G] ("G" for
  Get), choose a destination directory, and confirm. Press [ESC] to
  cancel.

==============================================================================
7. STREAMING MP3 & RADIO STATIONS
==============================================================================

- MP3s found via search sources can be streamed directly (no need
  to download first) -- this also enables listening to internet
  radio stations.
- Streaming uses UHCTools for network transport.
- The infobox shows the amount of data downloaded so far.

==============================================================================
8. WINDOW & FONT CUSTOMIZATION
==============================================================================

- Both the main window and the info window can be resized
  (horizontally and vertically) by dragging the resize gadget in
  the lower-right corner.
- Change fonts via Prefs > Display: one selector for the main/list
  font, another for the infobox and button fonts. Any font can be
  used (font restrictions have been removed).
- Enable "Big buttons" in Prefs for larger, easier-to-click gadgets
  (useful on high-resolution screens).
- Enable "Button tooltips" in Prefs to see a help popup when
  hovering over any gadget.

==============================================================================
9. POSITION SLIDER & PLAY MODE BUTTON
==============================================================================

- Enable Prefs > Display > Position slider to show a slider
  for viewing and jumping to a playback position (works for most
  module formats supporting pattern-skip, and for locally played
  MP3s).
- Enable "Play mode button" (Prefs > Display) to add a button next
  to the slider that cycles play modes (repeat, loop, random, etc.)
  without opening Prefs.

==============================================================================
10. SCOPES (VISUALIZERS)
==============================================================================

- Multiple scope types can run simultaneously (enable each
  independently in Prefs > Display):

  - Waveform-style scopes (HippoScope, QuadraScope, etc.) -- adjust
    size with "Scope size" in Prefs.
  - Spectrum -- frequency (X) vs. loudness in dB (Y).
  - Patternscope -- shows pattern data for 4-18 channels side by
    side; use XL mode for double-height rows.
    - For 8+ channels, install the "mini4" font (from Aminet) so
      channel labels fit.
  - PatternScope for PSID -- visualizes SID chip register state
    instead of a real pattern.

- Scope window positions/open states are remembered across
  sessions.
- Adjust "Scope priority" in Prefs if scopes stutter during
  CPU-heavy decoding (e.g. MP3).
- Toggle scopes with [Z].

==============================================================================
11. SID / PSID PLAYBACK
==============================================================================

- Configure output in Prefs > Play-2 > PlaySID mode:

  - Normal (original PlaySID emulation)
  - reSID 6581 / reSID 8580 (accurate emulation, needs a fast CPU)
  - reSID Auto (auto-selects chip version)
  - SIDBlaster / USBSID-Pico / ZorroSID (USB/hardware SID devices)
  - Trinity accelerator SID core (single/dual SID; requires
    suitable Trinity firmware)

- "reSID mode" settings let you pick filter behavior (Internal,
  Internal+Ext, All off) and oversampling for better sound quality.
- Supports mono, dual (2SID), and triple (3SID) SID setups.
- For extra song info, download STIL.txt and Songlengths.md5 from
  the HVSC site and place them in the Hippo directory:

  - Displays composer/title trivia (STIL) in the info window when
    playing files from an HVSC-structured path/URL.
  - Enables song length display and accurate end-of-song detection.

==============================================================================
12. HIGH-QUALITY XM PLAYBACK (XMAPLAY)
==============================================================================

- Enable in Prefs > Play-2 > Enable xmaplay -- a high-quality
  FastTracker 2 (XM) replayer alternative to the default PS3M-based
  one.
- Choose your output combination:

  - xmaplay + Paula   -- needs a 68060.
  - xmaplay + AHI     -- enable AHI in Prefs too.
  - xmaplay + AmiGUS  -- enable "Use AmiGUS hardware mixer" in Prefs;
                         runs fine even on 68000.

- Shows instrument names and channel count in the info
  window/infobox.

==============================================================================
13. MIDI PLAYBACK
==============================================================================

- Choose a mode in Prefs > Play-2 > MIDI mode:

  - Serial output -- via "delimidi", sends MIDI to external gear on
    the serial port.
  - Paula/AHI via Timidity -- good quality, CPU-heavy (68060
    recommended). Requires AmiTiMiDity unpacked and a "timidity:"
    assign.
  - Paula/AHI via GMPlay -- lighter on CPU (68020+). Requires GMPlay
    installed with a "gm:" assign and Patrik's file driver in
    gm:SoundDrivers.

==============================================================================
14. CONSOLE/CHIPTUNE MUSIC (VGM2WAV, MDX2WAV)
==============================================================================

- Install the vgm2wav tool (from Aminet) into C: or the Hippo
  directory to play: AY, GBS, GYM, HES, KSS, NSF/NSFE, SAP, SPC,
  VGM/VGZ formats (gzip required for .vgz).
- Install mdx2wav similarly to play MDX music (Sharp X68000, FM
  synth) -- an 060 may still not be fast enough for smooth
  playback.
- Both support scopes, subsongs, and song-end detection where
  applicable.

==============================================================================
15. MP3 VIA EXTERNAL HARDWARE (MHI)
==============================================================================

- Enable MHI in Prefs and select a suitable driver to play MP3s via
  dedicated MP3 decoder hardware (overrides MPEGA/AHI settings for
  MP3 files).

==============================================================================
16. AMIGUS HARDWARE MIXING
==============================================================================

- Requires amigus.library (works with both Zorro and PCMCIA AmiGUS
  cards).
- Enable Prefs > PS3M > Use AmiGUS hardware mixer to offload
  multichannel module mixing to the card's 32-channel hardware
  mixer.
- To play Protracker modules through AmiGUS, set Prefs > Play-1 >
  PT Replayer to PS3M.
- AmiGUS Mini is also supported.

==============================================================================
17. TRINITY ACCELERATOR AUDIO
==============================================================================

- Enable via PlaySID mode in Prefs (requires suitable Trinity
  firmware) for SID playback (single/dual core).
- Also supports playback of AY8910-chip VGM files (e.g. ZX Spectrum
  tunes from vgmrips.net).

==============================================================================
18. METADATA & SONG LENGTH DATABASE
==============================================================================

- Download songlengths.tsv and metadata.tsv (via the project's
  GitHub page: audacious-uade-tools > tsv > pretty > xxh32) and
  place them in the Hippo directory.
- On first start, Hippo converts them into au-songlengths.db /
  au-metadata.db (a one-time, somewhat slow process); the .tsv
  files can then be deleted.
- Once loaded, you get: song length in the title bar/position
  slider, author/publisher/album/year info in the infobox and info
  window, and automatic end-of-song detection for formats lacking
  native support. Data currently covers 300,000+ modules for
  metadata and 470,000+ for song lengths.

==============================================================================
19. NEW SUPPORTED MUSIC FORMATS
==============================================================================

Many formats were added over time -- notable additions include
Symphonie Pro, Sound Master, Sound Programming Language, Impulse
Tracker (v1.00/v2.00/v2.14), PreTracker, Mark Cooksey, Art of Noise
(4/8ch), and dozens of Eagleplayer-based formats (Rob Hubbard,
Jochen Hippel, TCBTracker, Quartet, etc.). Some formats need
external plugins/tools -- see the "Additional files" section of the
changelog for download links (e.g. "impulse" + "ImpulseDecruncher"
for Impulse Tracker, "Symphonie Pro" eagleplayer for Symphonie
modules). Check the full "List of supported formats" at the end of
the changelog for the complete list.

==============================================================================
20. KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS REFERENCE
==============================================================================

  SHIFT+M    Toggle list mode
  CTRL+F     Favorite/unfavorite selected module
  BACKSPACE  Go to parent directory (file browser)
  CTRL+S     Activate search / search modules
  CTRL+G     Download selected remote file
  CTRL+M     Search Modland
  F          Find in list
  SHIFT+F    Find next 
  A          Add selected item (file browser/search) to main list
  Z          Toggle scope
  DEL        Delete list item / go to parent (file browser)

==============================================================================
Guide compiled from the HippoPlayer changelog (v2.45 -> v2.67).
For hardware-specific setup (AmiGUS, SIDBlaster, Trinity, etc.) and
additional required tools/libraries, see the "Additional files to
check and download" section of the original readme.
